WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
- Hey y'all,

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.168
welcome to Is This Okay,

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:04.252
where we talk about things that people

00:00:04.252 --> 00:00:05.260
aren't talking about.

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:06.149
I'm Nyla.

00:00:06.149 --> 00:00:07.766
- Ooh, I'm Becky.

00:00:07.766 --> 00:00:08.599
- I'm Daysha.

00:00:08.599 --> 00:00:09.573
- I'm Chris.

00:00:09.573 --> 00:00:10.927
- And I'm Morgan.

00:00:10.927 --> 00:00:12.260
(group laughs)

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:13.093
- So, today,

00:00:13.093 --> 00:00:14.183
we'll be discussing

00:00:14.183 --> 00:00:18.350
Colin Kaepernick's recent
protest for every NFL game,

00:00:19.633 --> 00:00:21.929
due to racial injustice,

00:00:21.929 --> 00:00:23.279
everything that's happening in the world,

00:00:23.279 --> 00:00:25.270
where blacks are being killed by police,

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:27.798
and it's gaining nationwide attention.

00:00:27.798 --> 00:00:28.894
Other people have been doing it.

00:00:28.894 --> 00:00:32.362
Other NFL stars, I think there
are a few soccer players,

00:00:32.362 --> 00:00:35.665
and now, it's kind of branching
out towards high schools

00:00:35.665 --> 00:00:39.009
and, you know, so it's
getting a lot of attention.

00:00:39.009 --> 00:00:41.821
- We live in a country where
there's freedom of expression.

00:00:41.821 --> 00:00:44.862
And I don't even think that
this is a debate to be had.

00:00:44.862 --> 00:00:48.656
Like, if you don't believe in
what your government's doing,

00:00:48.656 --> 00:00:49.489
protest.

00:00:49.489 --> 00:00:51.186
Why are people up in arms about it?

00:00:51.186 --> 00:00:53.130
I mean, do we know why
people are so up in arms?

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:56.779
- A lot of it comes out
of disrespect for...

00:00:56.779 --> 00:00:58.096
- Veterans.
- Veterans.

00:00:58.096 --> 00:00:59.858
- America.
- Yeah, the military.

00:00:59.858 --> 00:01:02.413
- 9/11, and stuff like that.

00:01:02.413 --> 00:01:04.170
But at the same time, when you think about

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:05.641
the conversation on protest,

00:01:05.641 --> 00:01:06.770
it's like whoa, you know,

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:08.047
they always riot.

00:01:08.047 --> 00:01:10.067
And they steal, and they
loot, and they do whatever,

00:01:10.067 --> 00:01:11.301
so, it's like now,

00:01:11.301 --> 00:01:12.439
I think what's frustrating about this

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:14.099
is that you have an example of someone

00:01:14.099 --> 00:01:15.742
who's peacefully protesting.

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:18.205
Like, all he's doing,
is kneeling or sitting,

00:01:18.205 --> 00:01:20.205
and yet, people want to burn his jersey.

00:01:20.205 --> 00:01:22.304
They want to send him death threats.

00:01:22.304 --> 00:01:23.780
- I don't think he deserves death threats

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:25.385
and I don't think he
deserves to be attacked,

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:28.203
but I also do think that
the people, not all people,

00:01:28.203 --> 00:01:30.557
but some people who are
upset by his actions

00:01:30.557 --> 00:01:32.838
can't be completely disregarded,

00:01:32.838 --> 00:01:34.818
because I found myself very torn,

00:01:34.818 --> 00:01:36.251
because I realized in that moment,

00:01:36.251 --> 00:01:38.501
I was like, part of me wants to be like,

00:01:38.501 --> 00:01:40.425
"I'm always preaching
about you should be able to

00:01:40.425 --> 00:01:42.532
"protest peacefully, as
long as it's peaceful,"

00:01:42.532 --> 00:01:43.490
blah, blah, blah.

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:44.871
But then, we did this,

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:47.346
it also is a huge symbol, and so,

00:01:47.346 --> 00:01:51.314
I can't completely disregard
people who find it offensive.

00:01:51.314 --> 00:01:52.493
So, I was more, like, in the middle.

00:01:52.493 --> 00:01:54.710
- Yeah, I do feel like it is a matter

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:57.476
of people disagreeing with him.

00:01:57.476 --> 00:02:00.114
I don't think they bother looking at

00:02:00.114 --> 00:02:02.503
the nuance and the
actual reasons behind why

00:02:02.503 --> 00:02:03.591
he is doing what he's doing.

00:02:03.591 --> 00:02:06.250
- I was in New York City,
in lower Manhattan on 9/11.

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:07.800
There were people a lot closer than me,

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:11.776
but I was pretty damn in it for 9/11,

00:02:11.776 --> 00:02:13.939
and it was a fucking horrible day.

00:02:13.939 --> 00:02:18.377
And, I absolutely am
grateful to the military.

00:02:18.377 --> 00:02:20.287
I have family members
that are in the military.

00:02:20.287 --> 00:02:21.517
They fight for our country.

00:02:21.517 --> 00:02:22.588
That's amazing.

00:02:22.588 --> 00:02:24.300
They're selfless.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:25.550
I think that...

00:02:27.205 --> 00:02:29.309
Being proud of our country

00:02:29.309 --> 00:02:31.559
and feeling the patriotism,

00:02:32.967 --> 00:02:34.788
unity as a country,

00:02:34.788 --> 00:02:36.427
is not mutually exclusive,

00:02:36.427 --> 00:02:38.427
from saying there's something wrong here,

00:02:38.427 --> 00:02:40.189
and we need to do something about it,

00:02:40.189 --> 00:02:42.798
and someone like Colin
Kaepernick is in a position

00:02:42.798 --> 00:02:46.267
to take a knee and start
a national conversation.

00:02:46.267 --> 00:02:48.948
- He took a stand and didn't tell anybody,

00:02:48.948 --> 00:02:50.527
because he didn't wanna be stopped,

00:02:50.527 --> 00:02:51.543
and I think that's important,

00:02:51.543 --> 00:02:52.733
especially as a black American.

00:02:52.733 --> 00:02:54.457
When we fight for our rights,

00:02:54.457 --> 00:02:56.849
we should never have to ask permission,

00:02:56.849 --> 00:02:58.927
to corporate organizations,

00:02:58.927 --> 00:03:00.900
who are majority white men, saying like,

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:02.128
hey, is this okay?

00:03:02.128 --> 00:03:04.099
I am fighting for my
right, as a black American,

00:03:04.099 --> 00:03:06.769
because something is wrong,
and I have that right,

00:03:06.769 --> 00:03:08.008
as an American, to do so.

00:03:08.008 --> 00:03:09.979
- But, I think it's also important to note

00:03:09.979 --> 00:03:11.999
that when he decided instead of sitting,

00:03:11.999 --> 00:03:13.152
he was gonna take a knee,

00:03:13.152 --> 00:03:15.958
it was because he went
and had a conversation

00:03:15.958 --> 00:03:17.868
with a military elder.
- Exactly.

00:03:17.868 --> 00:03:20.399
- Yeah.
- He said that he agreed.

00:03:20.399 --> 00:03:22.216
There's a problem in this
country we need to fix,

00:03:22.216 --> 00:03:25.394
but, here's something that
we can do that's in between.

00:03:25.394 --> 00:03:27.124
- When you think about it, all it was

00:03:27.124 --> 00:03:30.424
was this guy, who was
against something that's

00:03:30.424 --> 00:03:31.942
obviously a problem,

00:03:31.942 --> 00:03:34.751
and all he was doing,
was just not standing,

00:03:34.751 --> 00:03:35.971
or putting his hand over his heart,

00:03:35.971 --> 00:03:37.158
for the national anthem.

00:03:37.158 --> 00:03:39.456
But, the fact that it went
from like, "He's an asshole,"

00:03:39.456 --> 00:03:41.276
to, "I want him to die."
- [Morgan] Right.

00:03:41.276 --> 00:03:42.826
- And people being like, "Good for him,"

00:03:42.826 --> 00:03:44.106
to like, "He is a god,"

00:03:44.106 --> 00:03:49.002
I think, shows how much the
country's upset right now.

00:03:49.002 --> 00:03:49.992
- [Morgan] Oh yeah.
- Because everyone just

00:03:49.992 --> 00:03:52.475
use that as this symbolic thing.

00:03:52.475 --> 00:03:53.624
- Yeah!
- He lit a fuse.

00:03:53.624 --> 00:03:54.825
- It's like this flagpole of patriotism.

00:03:54.825 --> 00:03:56.189
- It was huge!
- Yeah.

00:03:56.189 --> 00:03:57.268
- I mean, he even said he was like,

00:03:57.268 --> 00:03:58.156
"It's interesting to see

00:03:58.156 --> 00:04:00.406
"how racism, how patriotism

00:04:01.247 --> 00:04:04.298
"is being, kind of like the
cover for racism right now."

00:04:04.298 --> 00:04:05.131
- Oh my god!
- [Becky] Yeah!

00:04:05.131 --> 00:04:06.065
- [Morgan] Oh my god!
- And that was real!

00:04:06.065 --> 00:04:07.545
And that's true!
- Yeah, totally!

00:04:07.545 --> 00:04:09.075
- And like, a valid point is that,

00:04:09.075 --> 00:04:11.115
and this brings up a
whole other conversation,

00:04:11.115 --> 00:04:13.295
but the national anthem is racist.

00:04:13.295 --> 00:04:15.283
But, I mean, you can easily look it up.

00:04:15.283 --> 00:04:16.592
- Yeah.
- You can be like,

00:04:16.592 --> 00:04:18.388
national anthem, is it racist, or naw?

00:04:18.388 --> 00:04:19.804
And it will be like, yeah, it is!

00:04:19.804 --> 00:04:21.506
- Do we sing the...?
- No, we don't

00:04:21.506 --> 00:04:22.466
sing that part anymore.
- We don't sing that part,

00:04:22.466 --> 00:04:24.864
and that's why a lot of people
don't know that it's racist,

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:26.054
is because we don't sing that.

00:04:26.054 --> 00:04:27.215
- With all that said though,

00:04:27.215 --> 00:04:29.043
because the country's
never gonna be perfect,

00:04:29.043 --> 00:04:30.520
then our dues can never really allowed

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:31.547
to be patriotic?

00:04:31.547 --> 00:04:33.134
Like, I actually don't know the answer.

00:04:33.134 --> 00:04:35.604
I'm actually asking just
what do you guys think?

00:04:35.604 --> 00:04:36.437
- [Daysha] I don't know.

00:04:36.437 --> 00:04:38.907
I think I always think back
to early American history.

00:04:38.907 --> 00:04:41.522
And you think about how this
country was built on the fact

00:04:41.522 --> 00:04:43.711
that people threw tea into the water,

00:04:43.711 --> 00:04:44.651
and they said F this!

00:04:44.651 --> 00:04:46.160
Like, I'm not gonna do this!

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:48.450
And so, when I think about that,

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:49.942
and how that's how our country started,

00:04:49.942 --> 00:04:52.009
and then I think about
Kaepernick taking a knee,

00:04:52.009 --> 00:04:53.184
it's like, are you serious?
- Yeah.

00:04:53.184 --> 00:04:55.766
- Totally!
- I almost now feel like

00:04:55.766 --> 00:05:00.038
it feels weird, then, to ever
stand for the national anthem,

00:05:00.038 --> 00:05:02.343
unless the country is perfect,

00:05:02.343 --> 00:05:03.301
'cause I feel like every time,

00:05:03.301 --> 00:05:06.083
if you ever do stand for it,
are you ignoring the cause?

00:05:06.083 --> 00:05:08.410
- Right, are you, yeah.
- 'Cause if it's not

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:11.440
police brutality, it's rape.

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:13.568
It's, I don't know, it's
just tons of things.

00:05:13.568 --> 00:05:14.505
It's economic.

00:05:14.505 --> 00:05:15.338
It's justice.

00:05:15.338 --> 00:05:16.728
It's just all this other stuff,

00:05:16.728 --> 00:05:18.156
and so, at what point,

00:05:18.156 --> 00:05:20.295
should we never be doing that?

00:05:20.295 --> 00:05:21.903
Is that always disgraceful?

00:05:21.903 --> 00:05:23.923
- I mean, I think that as a society,

00:05:23.923 --> 00:05:26.512
we have an internal national gauge,

00:05:26.512 --> 00:05:27.845
that seems to go

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:31.158
how systemic is this problem?

00:05:31.158 --> 00:05:32.941
- I think another big problem too, though,

00:05:32.941 --> 00:05:34.900
is that we don't like to revisit things.

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:36.339
We don't really like to change things.

00:05:36.339 --> 00:05:39.573
So, it's like, you wanna say,
why don't you follow the law,

00:05:39.573 --> 00:05:42.362
and if you just follow the
law, you wouldn't get shot.

00:05:42.362 --> 00:05:44.060
- Who is the law written by?
- But, this law wasn't written

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:45.377
with me in mind.

00:05:45.377 --> 00:05:47.667
This law didn't see me as
a person to begin with.

00:05:47.667 --> 00:05:50.146
- Yeah.
- It never really had me

00:05:50.146 --> 00:05:52.036
in its center.

00:05:52.036 --> 00:05:53.446
So, that's kind of the problem,

00:05:53.446 --> 00:05:56.453
and I agree that we
need some kind of order.

00:05:56.453 --> 00:05:57.840
That's kind of how society works.

00:05:57.840 --> 00:06:00.650
But at the same time, why
can't we revisit these things?

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:01.483
- Yeah.
- Why can't we have

00:06:01.483 --> 00:06:02.521
conversations?

00:06:02.521 --> 00:06:06.640
- Alright, so I think that is
the end of today's episode.

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:09.754
Let us know what you guys
think in the comments below.

00:06:09.754 --> 00:06:11.452
And we'll see you guys next week.

00:06:11.452 --> 00:06:15.119
(relaxing electronic music)

